{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"a070a7fb333279e583164b2fc33cbe91d39f42624af2b4a6e25b2ff8e36c4590","slug":"ch03.standard-notations-copy","location":"/ch03/03-03-standard-notations copy.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"3.3 Standard notations and common functions","content_includes_title":false,"github":"https://github.com/jpowerj/clrs","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/jpowerj/clrs/blob/main/ch03/03-03-standard-notations copy.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/jpowerj/clrs/edit/main/ch03/03-03-standard-notations copy.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"03-03-standard-notations copy.md","url":"/03-03-standard-notat-2e2245a2fbf6ddc6b55924050f99acad.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This section reviews some standard mathematical functions and notations and explores the relationships among them. It also illustrates the use of the asymptotic notations.","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"MVNax6RhRy"}],"key":"fOvfYM9Kqd"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monotonicity","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"u3ht0HOc5C"}],"key":"FYIg23BJpU"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":8,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function f .n/ is monotonically increasing if m හ n implies f .m/ හ f .n/.\nSimilarly, it is monotonically decreasing if m හ n implies f .m/  f .n/. A func-\ntion f .n/ is strictly increasing if m < n implies f .m/ < f .n/ and strictly de-\ncreasing if m < n implies f .m/ > f .n/","position":{"start":{"line":8,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"key":"gP45L0tsAq"}],"key":"l0E4nKKY7l"}],"key":"cB5lE7r4Gj"}],"key